-- Align Self-Improvement with the error, learning, and feature-request workflow.
UPDATE skills
SET
  description = 'Captures verified errors, learnings, and feature requests as durable memory so the agent improves across future runs.',
  content = E'## Self-Improvement\n\nUse durable memory as a compact improvement log. Review relevant retrieved memories before significant work, and apply any applicable prevention rule.\n\nAfter a meaningful event, first handle the current task correctly. Then call `native_save_memory` once for each verified, reusable item:\n\n- **Error** — a command, tool, integration, or workflow fails unexpectedly. Save: `[Error] Area: <area>. Failure: <brief failure>. Cause: <verified cause>. Prevention: <specific action>.`\n- **Learning** — the user corrects you, knowledge was outdated, or you discover a better repeatable approach. Save: `[Learning: correction|knowledge_gap|best_practice] Area: <area>. Rule: <what to do or avoid>.`\n- **Feature request** — the user requests a capability that does not exist or would materially improve the product. Save: `[Feature Request] Capability: <requested capability>. Need: <why it matters>. Suggested direction: <brief implementation idea, if known>.`\n\nUse a compact, self-contained rule, not a transcript. Set `reason` to the trigger (for example, `user correction` or `verified tool failure`). Use `importance_score` of 0.85–0.95 for high-impact errors or corrections, 0.75–0.84 for reusable best practices and recurring feature requests, and never below 0.70. If a related memory is already retrieved or the result is a routine retry, do not save a duplicate.\n\nWhen a logged error or request is resolved, save a new compact follow-up: `[Resolved] <topic>. Resolution: <what changed>. Prevention: <durable rule>.` Do not claim a memory was saved unless `native_save_memory` succeeds; do not announce saves unless asked.\n\nDo not save secrets, tokens, private keys, raw logs, full transcripts, sensitive personal data, transient task state, routine one-off requests, unverified hypotheses, or failures whose cause is unknown. Verify uncertain lessons before storing them. Memory supports recall and deduplication; it is not a replacement for issue tracking, audit logs, or a full error database.',
  required_tool_names = ARRAY['native_save_memory'],
  updated_at = NOW()
WHERE workspace_id IS NULL AND name = 'Self-Improvement';
